> figure1 = ggplot()+
>     geom_point(data=DF, aes(x=day, y=temp))+
>     annotate('text', x=5, y=2, label='y= ax + b, R2=0.95')
> print(figure1)

> --

​Rather than "upper case 2", I think you mean "superscript 2" (as in R-squared or R² ). The superscript 2 character is unicode charater U+00B2. In the normal R CLI on Windows 7 Professional (at work), I was able to put in the
²
​ by holding down the <ALT> key while pressing the ​0178 keys in that order, then releasing the <ALT> key. But, perhaps better, is to use "R\u{00B2}". If I have indeed understood what you want, please try:

​
figure1 = ggplot()+
    geom_point(data=DF, aes(x=day, y=temp))+

    annotate('text', x=5, y=2, label='y= ax + b, R

​\u{00B2}​
=0.95')
print(figure1)

--
Heisenberg may have been here.

Unicode: http://xkcd.com/1726/

Maranatha! <><
John McKown

